  "title": "Notify After 'Best Answer' has been cancelled ?",
  "content": "<p>So I’ve had <strong>three </strong>notifications that a ‘Best Answer’ has been selected on this thread - two of them were <em>my</em> answer - but it currently has NO ‘Best’ answer!</p><figure><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://uploads-eu-west-1.insided.com/stmicroelectronics-en/attachment/e028270a-f128-4658-8dfa-5317e9afaa53.png\" /></figure><p><oembed url=\"https://community.st.com/stm32-mcus-products-25/minimum-current-requirement-for-external-vref-on-stm32g474-167348\"></oembed></p><p> </p><p>If a Notification is seen as necessary when a ‘Best Answer’ has been marked, shouldn’t one also be provided if it gets unmarked - especially when it is one’s own answer?!</p><p> </p><p><strong><u>PS</u>:</strong></p><p>The reason for the multiple Notifications (and, presumably, for the mark to have disappeared at the time of the screenshot) is given here:</p><oembed url=\"https://community.st.com/feedback-forum-118/what-s-going-on-with-these-multiple-best-answer-notifications-167361?postid=745987#post745987\"></oembed><p> </p>",
